"""Verifier for the stage run-ledger repair task.

Visible tier: the stage-1 outputs under /app/out are compared, exactly, with the
ledger the approved rules produce from the shipped feed (computed at build time
and embedded below; the verifier container has no /app/data).

Hidden tier: a stage-2 feed is regenerated here by generate_feed (the plain-Python
generator below; stdlib, openpyxl and pyarrow only, no network, no subprocess) from
the parameters and seed in _EVAL_INPUTS_B64 with the same documented rules, the
delivered package is run on it with the agent's own resume_state.json as opening
state, and its outputs are compared exactly with the embedded expectation.  Fresh
keys, values and trap placements, same rules.

Embedded data (base64 of zlib-compressed JSON, never executed): _EXPECTED_B64 holds
the expected stage-1 and stage-2 outputs; _EVAL_INPUTS_B64 holds the generator inputs.

Negative checks hold when the cheat happened; their negative weight subtracts.
"""

